{"qid":"Q766","names":["Jamaica"],"title":"Jamaica","endonym":{"native":"Jamaica","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Jamaica achieved independence from the United Kingdom on 6 August 1962, withdrawing from the short-lived Federation of the West Indies and establishing a Westminster-model parliamentary constitutional monarchy with the British Crown represented by a local Governor-General. Under the first Prime Minister Alexander Bustamante of the Jamaica Labour Party, the new state joined the United Nations immediately and pursued non-aligned foreign policy. Despite chronic economic challenges and periodic political violence, Jamaica exercised substantial global cultural influence as the birthplace of reggae, ska, dancehall, and the Rastafari movement, and produced athletes of exceptional international standing.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Jamaica's territorial extent as an island state is precisely defined; the dataset records its sovereign period from 1963 onward, the slight offset from the August 1962 independence date likely reflecting a data-source convention.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Jamaica","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaica"},{"label":"Britannica: Jamaica","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Jamaica"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Independence of Jamaica","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independence_of_Jamaica"}],"britannica":"place/Jamaica","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Jamaica","rulers":[{"qid":"Q9682","name":"Elizabeth II","start":1962,"end":2022,"image":"Queen Elizabeth II official portrait for 1959 tour (retouched) (cropped) (3-to-4 aspect ratio).jpg","imageUrl":"htt